@startuml HermesDocumentService
allowmixing
title hermes-document-service: high-level dependencies (proposal)
top to bottom direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 65
hide empty members

class "main" as Main <<bootstrap>> {
  load configuration
  construct application objects and adapters
  inject selected implementations
  start server; coordinate graceful shutdown
}
package "Presentation" {
  class "internal/api" as API {
    HTTP OR gRPC handlers
    decode requests / validate DTOs / map errors
    Auth / Users / Workspaces / Documents
  }
  class "internal/api/session" as Middleware {
    extract opaque session token
    validate session; pass authenticated identity
  }
}
class "internal/app" as App {
  Auth / Users / Workspaces / Documents
  orchestrate use cases and domain transactions
  consumer-owned repository and adapter interfaces
}
class "internal/domain" as Domain {
  User / Credentials / Workspace / Membership
  Invitation / Document / Subscription
  access policies / invariants / version conflicts
  domain events and application errors
}
package "Infrastructure adapters" {
  class "internal/postgres" as Postgres {
    UnitOfWork and transactional repositories
    users / credentials / workspaces / memberships
    invitations / documents / subscriptions
  }
  class "internal/redis" as Redis {
    SessionStore implementation
    create / validate / revoke active sessions
    versioned shared contract for HDS and HNS
  }
  class "internal/credentials" as Credentials {
    CredentialVerifier implementation
    prepare / verify credential data
    authentication method remains open
  }
  class "internal/kafka" as Kafka {
    DomainEventPublisher implementation
    serialize and publish domain facts
    publication protocol remains open (ADR-002)
  }
}
package "External infrastructure" {
  database "PostgreSQL\nDomain data" as DB
  database "Redis\nActive sessions" as Sessions
  queue "Kafka\nDomain events to notification-service" as Events
}
package "Proposed extensions" {
  class "internal/app/settings" as Settings {
    user settings use cases (ADR-003)
    PostgreSQL persistence + versioned Redis state
    synchronize changes through an owned interface
  }
  class "internal/redis/settings" as SettingsAdapter {
    settings representation + explicit Pub/Sub signal
    UserSettingsChanged(user_id, version)
    retry / reconciliation protocol remains open
  }
}

Main -down-> API : create and serve
Main -down-> App : construct and inject adapters
API -right-> Middleware : protected operations
Middleware -down-> App : Auth.ValidateSession
API -down-> App : invoke use cases
App -left-> Domain : apply policies and invariants
App -down-> Postgres : uses UnitOfWork / repository contracts
App -down-> Redis : uses SessionStore contract
App -right-> Credentials : uses CredentialVerifier contract
App -down-> Kafka : uses DomainEventPublisher contract
Postgres ..> Domain : map stored entities
Postgres -down-> DB : read / write; commit / rollback
Redis -down-> Sessions : session lifecycle
Kafka -down-> Events : publish
API ..> Settings : proposed settings operations
Settings ..> Postgres : proposed durable settings repository
Settings ..> SettingsAdapter : proposed synchronization contract
SettingsAdapter ..> Sessions : proposed versioned state + Pub/Sub

note top of Main
  Creation happens here; runtime requests do not pass through main.
  Bootstrap owns infrastructure connections and shutdown order.
end note
note bottom of App
  Authentication establishes identity; domain operations check current access.
  Registration creates user + personal workspace + owner membership
  in one PostgreSQL transaction. Domain mutations check expected_version.
  PostgreSQL and Redis do not share a transaction: account deletion and
  session revocation require a separate coordination protocol (ADR-001).
end note
note bottom of Kafka
  Kafka is the accepted event channel, not a delivery guarantee.
  Direct post-commit publication versus outbox/CDC remains open.
  An outbox worker and atomic event persistence must be detailed
  if that option is selected; they are not assumed by this diagram.
end note
legend bottom
  Proposed Go package structure; server code is not implemented yet.
  Boxes group responsibilities; they are not additional Go classes.
  App owns interfaces; infrastructure adapters implement them.
  Adapter arrows show injected runtime dependencies, not concrete Go imports.
  Fake adapters can be injected in application tests.
  Solid links: base dependency structure; dotted links to settings: proposal.
  Sessions live in Redis, not PostgreSQL (ADR-001).
  API transport and credential method are not selected.
  HNS authorization access is open; no internal authorization API is assumed.
  User scenarios: scenarios/users.puml; authentication: scenarios/auth.puml.
endlegend
@enduml
